  "memorial_details": "A metal plaque mounted on a back board, the plaque has a colour badge of 97 Squadron RAF at top centre, and either side are lightly etched depictions of two Lancaster aircraft. The inscription is below with names in two columns by aircraft crew, all etched and in white.\n\nA memorial plaque was unveiled on 23 June 2014 at the crash site, commemorating the 13 crew members.\n\nMemorial Plaque Unveiling: The plaque commemorates Lancasters ME625 and ND981. It is unclear from the text if this event was a specific unveiling ceremony or just the general existence of the memorial.\n\nUnveiling of the Memorial (23 June 2014): Memorial unveiled to commemorate the 13 crew members who died in a mid-air collision on 23 June 1944.\n\nThe text describes a memorial dedicated to Lancasters ME625 and ND981, two World War II bombers. The memorial includes plaques with inscriptions detailing the aircraft's history and service during the war.",
